								"dir": "auto"
							},
							"content": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"text": "Whenever an EC2 instance sends traffic, AWS checks the route table associated with the subnet. Based on the destination IP, AWS selects the most specific matching route and forwards the traffic to the corresponding target such as local VPC, Internet Gateway, NAT Gateway, VPC Peering, or VPN. The route table determines the path of the traffic, while Security Groups and NACLs determine whether the traffic is allowed."
								}
							]
						}
					]
				}
			},
